r, and a 4000 pound cattle feeder was blown about 850 feet to the north-northeast. Two structures on the southeast side of Truscott-Brine Lake received roof and window damage. Utility poles were broken from the area just southeast of Truscott-Brine Lake to State Highway 6, including steel utility poles that were bent. The tornado weakened and then dissipated after crossing Highway 6.","source":"NWS Storm Survey","state":"TX","torLengthMi":8.4,"torScale":"EF3","torWidthYd":400.0,"type":"Tornado","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2021-04-27T20:50Z","county":"Knox","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-27T20:50Z","endLat":33.75,"endLon":-99.86,"episode":157752,"id":956153,"injuries":0,"lat":33.75,"location":"2.87 W Truscott","lon":-99.86,"magnitude":2.0,"source":"COOP Observer","state":"TX","type":"Hail","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2021-04-27T20:50Z","county":"Knox","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-27T20:50Z","endLat":33.75,"endLon":-99.86,"episode":157752,"id":956154,"injuries":0,"lat":33.75,"location":"2.87 W Truscott","lon":-99.86,"magnitude":52.0,"magnitudeType":"EG","narrative":"Estimated by observer.","source":"COOP Observer","state":"TX","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2021-04-27T21:03Z","county":"Knox","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-27T21:03Z","endLat":33.73,"endLon":-99.79,"episode":157752,"id":956155,"injuries":0,"lat":33.73,"location":"1.8 SE Truscott","lon":-99.79,"magnitude":60.0,"magnitudeType":"MG","source":"Mesonet","state":"TX","type":"Thunderstorm Wind","wfo":"OUN"},{"begin":"2021-04-27T21:21Z","county":"Olmsted","damageCrops":"0.00K","damageProperty":"0.00K","deaths":0,"end":"2021-04-27T21:21Z","endLat":44.03,"endLon":-92.64,"episode":157525,"id":952218,"injuries":0,"lat":44.03,"location":"0.5 E Byron","lon":-92.64,"magnitude":0.75,"source":"Broadcast Media","state":"MN","type":"Hail","wfo":"ARX"},{"begin":"2021-04-27T21:23Z","county